# Public Domain — RBI Forex Reference Rates

The files in this repository are a compilation of **facts**: Reserve Bank of
India reference exchange rates (numbers, dates, and currency codes), with no
original expression.

Copyright in India (Copyright Act, 1957) subsists only in **original** works
and requires a *modicum of creativity*. A bare compilation of factual data
lacks that originality and is therefore not copyrightable. This is the
principle affirmed in **Eastern Book Company v. D.B. Modak**, (2008) 1 SCC 1,
in which the Supreme Court of India held that factual data, absent original
expression, is not protected by copyright.

Accordingly, this dataset is in the **public domain** in India and, as far as
the author is aware, internationally.

To make the public-domain status explicit and enforceable everywhere, the
repository is additionally dedicated to the public domain under the **CC0 1.0
Universal (CC0 1.0) Public Domain Dedication**:

> https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

You may copy, modify, distribute, and use the data for any purpose — including
commercial purposes — without attribution or permission, and without any
warranty.
